# TAK Portal FeatureLink module — component-level ignores.
#
# This file did not previously exist (audit Appendix E §2.1). The root .gitignore also had
# no `node_modules/` rule of its own — only CloudTAK/.gitignore did — so an `npm install`
# run inside this directory would have staged thousands of files. Both halves are now fixed:
# the root file carries `**/node_modules/`, and this file carries the Node/Express specifics.
#
# Everything the root .gitignore already covers (OS junk, editor state, logs, .env) is NOT
# repeated here. Only genuine component deltas belong in this file.

# ── Node ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.npm/
npm-debug.log*

# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored — it is what makes `npm ci` reproducible
# in .github/workflows/ci.yml and is the input to this component's CycloneDX SBOM (C-30).

# ── Runtime / instance state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The module writes uploaded display-config datasets and unpacked custom icon sets under
# the portal's data root at runtime. Nothing generated at runtime belongs in the index.
uploads/
tmp/
data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# ── Install-script backups ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# install.sh rewrites files in the host portal in place; the remediated version writes a
# timestamped backup beside each file it patches. Those backups are host state, not source.
*.featurelink-backup
*.featurelink-backup.*

# ── Test / coverage output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
